1
00:03:16,644 --> 00:03:18,819
Stay together, let's go!

2
00:03:25,274 --> 00:03:28,034
Blow through the window.

3
00:04:43,593 --> 00:04:45,906
Uh oh, here comes trouble.

4
00:04:49,841 --> 00:04:51,428
You could've killed him.

5
00:04:51,429 --> 00:04:53,603
Yeah, you need a lawyer?

6
00:04:55,053 --> 00:04:58,089
Hey, never ever
let go of that hose.

7
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:01,265
It's your lifeline, the way out.

8
00:05:01,266 --> 00:05:03,405
You're lucky
I don't need a coroner.

9
00:05:03,406 --> 00:05:05,269
I'm sorry, [mumbles].

10
00:05:05,270 --> 00:05:06,408
You shouldn't be
on your leg, man.

11
00:05:06,409 --> 00:05:08,100
Nah, I'll be fine.

12
00:05:14,728 --> 00:05:18,007
Don't ask me to stop
doin' what I love.

13
00:05:19,836 --> 00:05:22,355
All I've ever wanted to
do was drive that truck.

14
00:05:22,356 --> 00:05:25,531
My pops, his pops, and now me.

15
00:05:25,532 --> 00:05:26,360
Okay?

16
00:05:28,949 --> 00:05:29,777
Okay.

17
00:05:36,405 --> 00:05:39,615
I don't know about
your friend here.

18
00:05:48,727 --> 00:05:50,797
You really oughta do
somethin' about that asthma.

19
00:05:50,798 --> 00:05:53,352
Don't try and
change the subject.

20
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:56,665
I'm just thinkin' maybe
I'm not cut out for this.

21
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:58,702
I thought you
loved bein' a fireman.

22
00:05:58,703 --> 00:06:00,151
I do.

23
00:06:00,152 --> 00:06:03,120
The rush, the excitement,
it's got its perks.

24
00:06:03,121 --> 00:06:04,880
Then what's the problem?

25
00:06:04,881 --> 00:06:06,123
Yeah, see?

26
00:06:06,124 --> 00:06:08,263
People don't think
about the ugly side.

27
00:06:08,264 --> 00:06:12,406
They just fall in love with
the uniform, but it's not easy.

28
00:06:13,787 --> 00:06:18,100
You just gotta find a
place in your mind to put it.

29
00:06:18,101 --> 00:06:20,828
Yeah, some of
the things we see

30
00:06:22,002 --> 00:06:24,659
trust me you don't
wanna remember.

31
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:27,247
I just feel like
somethin's missin'.

32
00:06:27,248 --> 00:06:29,354
Well, you better decide

33
00:06:31,183 --> 00:06:33,426
'cause this is your life.

34
00:06:33,427 --> 00:06:36,292
Yeah, try tellin'
that to Spoon.

35
00:07:06,909 --> 00:07:09,876
Two days in the air
finally caught up with me.

36
00:07:09,877 --> 00:07:11,638
Yeah, I could tell.

37
00:07:14,019 --> 00:07:15,504
Another horoscope?

38
00:07:17,575 --> 00:07:20,542
"Take a look in the
mirror, let go of the past

39
00:07:20,543 --> 00:07:23,131
"and focus on the here and now.

40
00:07:23,132 --> 00:07:25,651
"Your life depends on it."

41
00:07:25,652 --> 00:07:27,411
That's common sense.

42
00:07:27,412 --> 00:07:28,757
That's your horoscope.

43
00:07:28,758 --> 00:07:30,828
The problem is you don't listen.

44
00:07:30,829 --> 00:07:33,728
Waste of paper and good ink.

45
00:07:33,729 --> 00:07:37,352
It's the stars that
make the world go 'round.

46
00:07:37,353 --> 00:07:38,181
What?

47
00:07:41,150 --> 00:07:43,703
Are you ever gonna paint again?

48
00:07:43,704 --> 00:07:45,602
Are you ever gonna
finish that book

49
00:07:45,603 --> 00:07:48,708
you've been writin'
for damn near a decade?

50
00:07:48,709 --> 00:07:50,539
Seven years and yes.

51
00:07:52,955 --> 00:07:55,371
They say poetry doesn't sell.

52
00:07:58,650 --> 00:08:02,342
The Arms Association
is having an art show.

53
00:08:02,343 --> 00:08:04,483
I think you should
enter somethin'.

54
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:07,486
Yeah, I lost to my passion.

55
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:11,351
Well it's my job to
help you get it back.

56
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:14,701
- Hey, hey!
- Hey.

57
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:16,944
Ah, this guy.

58
00:08:18,014 --> 00:08:20,119
the perfect life.

59
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:22,225
Yup, five years strong.

60
00:08:24,780 --> 00:08:25,745
Happy anniversary.

61
00:08:25,746 --> 00:08:27,506
Ooh, thank you!

62
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:28,508
Yeah, man.

63
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:34,098
It just keeps playin'
over and over in my mind.

64
00:08:34,099 --> 00:08:37,101
Sometimes it's hard to shake.

65
00:08:37,102 --> 00:08:39,241
I've been doing this
a lot longer than you.

66
00:08:39,242 --> 00:08:41,278
It comes with the territory.

67
00:08:41,279 --> 00:08:42,728
Trust me.

68
00:08:42,729 --> 00:08:43,660
You're gonna see a lot of things

69
00:08:43,661 --> 00:08:45,938
you wish you could forget.

70
00:08:45,939 --> 00:08:47,180
I coulda got a lifetime

71
00:08:47,181 --> 00:08:50,114
without seein' that
old guy like that.

72
00:08:50,115 --> 00:08:52,047
Old guy was homeless, man.

73
00:08:52,048 --> 00:08:53,532
Somebody loved him.

74
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,326
Don't matter now.

75
00:08:55,327 --> 00:08:56,156
Nope.

76
00:08:58,745 --> 00:09:00,469
Listenin' to his tales about

77
00:09:00,470 --> 00:09:04,922
when he worked on Wall
Street, did you believe him?

78
00:09:04,923 --> 00:09:06,372
Yeah, I did.

79
00:09:06,373 --> 00:09:07,649
Did you?

80
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:08,857
Hell naw.

81
00:09:08,858 --> 00:09:12,793
Well he's gone now.

82
00:09:14,415 --> 00:09:15,796
Just like that.

83
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:19,834
You know that's my biggest fear.

84
00:09:19,835 --> 00:09:21,836
Bein' homeless?

85
00:09:21,837 --> 00:09:23,010
Dyin' alone.

86
00:09:25,841 --> 00:09:29,153
So you love him,
or is it the fact

87
00:09:29,154 --> 00:09:31,949
that he'll be Marlon Jones MD

88
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:36,505
that keeps you waiting for
a man that's miles away?

89
00:09:36,506 --> 00:09:38,128
I love him.

90
00:09:38,129 --> 00:09:41,441
Has he asked you
to marry him yet?

91
00:09:41,442 --> 00:09:43,340
Do you see a ring?

92
00:09:43,341 --> 00:09:44,790
What about Caleb?

93
00:09:44,791 --> 00:09:47,586
Girl, he's got Breanna.

94
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:49,035
She is successful.

95
00:09:49,036 --> 00:09:50,381
She's bright,

96
00:09:50,382 --> 00:09:52,832
except when it comes to him.

97
00:09:52,833 --> 00:09:56,284
Yeah, I don't know why she
puts up with him exactly.

98
00:09:56,285 --> 00:09:57,734
Uh--

99
00:09:57,735 --> 00:09:59,045
Okay, maybe I do.

100
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:02,566
I could only
think of one reason.

101
00:10:02,567 --> 00:10:05,225
She loves his crusty underuse.

102
00:10:06,364 --> 00:10:08,434
He just hasn't found
the right one yet.

103
00:10:08,435 --> 00:10:12,612
He hasn't found the right
one because he's not looking.

104
00:10:14,268 --> 00:10:18,341
Mmm, mmm, mmm, my baby
sure can cook can't she?

105
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,861
Jack of all trades.

106
00:10:21,862 --> 00:10:23,587
How did I get so lucky?

107
00:10:23,588 --> 00:10:24,450
The uniform.

108
00:10:28,006 --> 00:10:31,319
Guess who I ran
into at the gym?

109
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,631
Asia

110
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:33,460
Redmon?

111
00:10:34,668 --> 00:10:38,084
Yeah, I guess she's
not Redmon anymore.

112
00:10:38,085 --> 00:10:41,363
I guess.

113
00:10:41,364 --> 00:10:45,541
Didn't she marry
that pilot?

114
00:10:48,268 --> 00:10:50,339
So that's funny to you?

115
00:10:51,236 --> 00:10:53,722
I'm just givin' information.

116
00:10:59,969 --> 00:11:02,074
Alright, aight.

117
00:11:02,075 --> 00:11:03,385
Whoa!

118
00:11:03,386 --> 00:11:06,768
I'm okay.

119
00:11:06,769 --> 00:11:09,426
He just had to bring that up.

120
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:20,333
I'm disappointed
in you Caleb Abrams.

121
00:11:20,334 --> 00:11:21,990
He had it comin', ma.

122
00:11:21,991 --> 00:11:24,166
Maybe he did, but still.

123
00:11:25,374 --> 00:11:28,583
Baby, when are you
gonna let this go?

124
00:11:28,584 --> 00:11:32,726
I just can't see myself
lovin' somebody all new.

125
00:11:33,934 --> 00:11:36,625
I know what it's
like to be in love

126
00:11:36,626 --> 00:11:39,905
and it's not supposed
to feel like that.

127
00:11:39,906 --> 00:11:42,702
Can't believe
it's been a year.

128
00:11:43,737 --> 00:11:45,634
Apologize to Bryce.

129
00:11:45,635 --> 00:11:47,222
He brought it on hisself.

130
00:11:47,223 --> 00:11:49,224
Apologize anyway.

131
00:11:49,225 --> 00:11:51,951
You guys have been
friends since childhood.

132
00:11:51,952 --> 00:11:54,367
So?

133
00:11:54,368 --> 00:11:57,716
So part of bein' a man is
acceptin' responsibilities

134
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:00,789
and that includes
saying you're sorry.

135
00:12:02,307 --> 00:12:05,033
You're startin'
to sound like Spoon.

136
00:12:05,034 --> 00:12:06,655
You need to call your dad.

137
00:12:06,656 --> 00:12:08,105
I don't feel like
hearing his mouth.

138
00:12:08,106 --> 00:12:10,695
Hey, that's still your daddy.

139
00:12:13,663 --> 00:12:17,598
Now let's eat some of
this cake while it's hot.

140
00:12:20,705 --> 00:12:24,950
Haven't seen you in
church in a month of Sundays.

141
00:12:24,951 --> 00:12:27,711
Not that long.

142
00:12:37,722 --> 00:12:40,206
You too busy for the Lord?

143
00:12:40,207 --> 00:12:43,658
No Spoon, you know
better than that.

144
00:12:43,659 --> 00:12:46,350
Is this painting gonna
get you into Heaven?

145
00:12:46,351 --> 00:12:48,111
Probably not.

146
00:12:48,112 --> 00:12:49,768
Neither is fighting fires.

147
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:52,184
Time I was your
age, I had you.

148
00:12:52,185 --> 00:12:53,358
I was married.

149
00:12:54,290 --> 00:12:56,119
What you tryin' to say, Spoon?

150
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,053
It's time to grow up.

151
00:13:01,021 --> 00:13:03,229
This is my life.

152
00:13:27,082 --> 00:13:28,565
Get out of here!

153
00:13:28,566 --> 00:13:30,498
When I tell you to get out
of there, that's what I mean!

154
00:13:30,499 --> 00:13:31,913
You split up the team!

155
00:13:31,914 --> 00:13:33,708
You put us all in jeopardy!

156
00:13:33,709 --> 00:13:36,745
If this had been a real
fire, you'd be dead!

157
00:13:36,746 --> 00:13:37,885
Strike two!

158
00:14:02,703 --> 00:14:03,703
What are you doin' here?

159
00:14:03,704 --> 00:14:04,635
What now?

160
00:14:04,636 --> 00:14:05,809
I wanted to surprise you.

161
00:14:05,810 --> 00:14:07,362
What, did you
think it was Imani?

162
00:14:07,363 --> 00:14:08,881
Come on, that's my roommate.

163
00:14:08,882 --> 00:14:10,745
Plus she got her own
bed and her own room.

164
00:14:10,746 --> 00:14:13,127
- Yeah, she better.
- You did surprise me though.

165
00:14:13,128 --> 00:14:14,438
- I did?
- Yeah, you did.

166
00:14:14,439 --> 00:14:17,857
I did surprise you
'cause I missed you.

167
00:14:19,824 --> 00:14:20,789
Did you miss me?

168
00:14:20,790 --> 00:14:22,067
I missed you, boy.

169
00:14:22,068 --> 00:14:24,864
Show me how much
you missed me.

170
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:28,937
So, lemme hear it.

171
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:31,801
Hear what?

172
00:14:34,218 --> 00:14:37,945
Not a word from you in
days, what's your excuse?

173
00:14:37,946 --> 00:14:40,396
I didn't know I needed one.

174
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:45,885
One day I'm gonna break
up with you for good.

175
00:14:47,334 --> 00:14:48,887
I thought you loved me.

176
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:50,303
I do sometimes.

177
00:14:51,718 --> 00:14:53,615
That's not what you
were sayin' a minute ago.

178
00:14:53,616 --> 00:14:55,446
Is that all this is?

179
00:14:57,103 --> 00:14:58,758
What more do you
want from me, girl?

180
00:14:58,759 --> 00:15:01,485
I can't keep doin'
this wit you, Caleb.

181
00:15:01,486 --> 00:15:02,729
Do you love me?

182
00:15:05,042 --> 00:15:06,733
I just showed you.

183
00:15:11,496 --> 00:15:13,635
You know what I think?

184
00:15:13,636 --> 00:15:16,984
I think you waitin'
for her to come back.

185
00:15:16,985 --> 00:15:18,503
Tell me I'm wrong.

186
00:15:29,411 --> 00:15:31,343
You shouldn't have let her in.

187
00:15:31,344 --> 00:15:33,690
I think you should
give her a chance.

188
00:15:33,691 --> 00:15:35,450
A chance for what?

189
00:15:35,451 --> 00:15:37,556
I don't know, to grow on you.

190
00:15:37,557 --> 00:15:38,730
Like fungus?

191
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:42,112
I don't know
but at some point,

192
00:15:42,113 --> 00:15:45,565
you're gonna have to
let your guard down.

193
00:15:58,060 --> 00:15:59,612
As much as your
head is in that book,

194
00:15:59,613 --> 00:16:03,340
you should know everything
there is to know about history.

195
00:16:03,341 --> 00:16:04,860
That's the plan.

196
00:16:09,347 --> 00:16:13,247
I can't believe I'm
about to be a dad.

197
00:16:13,248 --> 00:16:16,008
What if I'm not good at it?

198
00:16:16,009 --> 00:16:17,528
What if you are?

199
00:16:19,323 --> 00:16:21,670
You're gonna be a great dad.

200
00:16:23,534 --> 00:16:26,640
- I'm a good husband.
- Yes, you are.

201
00:16:28,021 --> 00:16:30,505
Still, I'm a little scared.

202
00:16:30,506 --> 00:16:33,508
You run into burnin'
buildings for a living.

203
00:16:33,509 --> 00:16:35,545
This is different.

204
00:16:35,546 --> 00:16:36,822
Yeah, well either way it goes,

205
00:16:36,823 --> 00:16:40,343
you're responsible
for a human life.

206
00:16:40,344 --> 00:16:43,311
I don't feel like
that goin' into a fire.

207
00:16:43,312 --> 00:16:45,175
Can't afford to be scared.

208
00:16:45,176 --> 00:16:47,419
I might not make it out.

209
00:17:14,378 --> 00:17:18,243
Suppose he doesn't
ask you to marry him.

210
00:17:18,244 --> 00:17:20,417
Then I guess I'm
stuck with you.

211
00:17:20,418 --> 00:17:23,282
Wow, is that such a bad thing?

212
00:17:23,283 --> 00:17:25,733
I pay my half of
the bills at least.

213
00:17:25,734 --> 00:17:27,736
That's more than most.

214
00:17:29,393 --> 00:17:32,568
Look, just don't
bet the farm on it.

215
00:17:34,363 --> 00:17:36,364
Why would you say that?

216
00:17:36,365 --> 00:17:39,988
Because you should be spendin'
this time writin' your book

217
00:17:39,989 --> 00:17:42,508
instead of wastin'
your time on this.

218
00:17:42,509 --> 00:17:44,959
Well who asked you?

219
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,030
I'm just sayin'.

220
00:17:47,031 --> 00:17:50,999
Thank God I'm gonna
be gone a few days.

221
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,382
That means I get
the house to myself?

222
00:17:54,383 --> 00:17:55,694
Yeah.

223
00:17:55,695 --> 00:17:56,523
Ooh.

224
00:18:08,949 --> 00:18:09,778
Asia.

225
00:18:10,917 --> 00:18:12,952
You look like
you've seen a ghost.

226
00:18:12,953 --> 00:18:15,094
What are you doin' here?

227
00:18:18,304 --> 00:18:20,478
I came to say I'm sorry.

228
00:18:22,273 --> 00:18:23,550
A year later?

229
00:18:24,724 --> 00:18:26,414
You weren't ready, Caleb.

230
00:18:26,415 --> 00:18:27,622
I wasn't ready?

231
00:18:27,623 --> 00:18:30,004
You tried to
find your passion.

232
00:18:30,005 --> 00:18:31,558
I needed stability.

233
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:36,010
And you didn't believe in me.

234
00:18:36,011 --> 00:18:37,599
I made a mistake.

235
00:18:41,016 --> 00:18:44,571
I made a mistake when
I opened that door.

236
00:19:17,570 --> 00:19:18,639
No table talking.

237
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:21,055
No table talking.
- Shh.

238
00:19:21,056 --> 00:19:24,265
Excuse me, we have
an announcement.

239
00:19:24,266 --> 00:19:25,508
Bam.

240
00:19:27,614 --> 00:19:29,581
Hold up, hold up, hold up.

241
00:19:29,582 --> 00:19:30,686
Got a prenup?

242
00:19:31,998 --> 00:19:33,171
- Really?
- What?

243
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,379
- Are you serious?
- Seriously?

244
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:36,174
Half of all marriages
end in divorce.

245
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:38,003
Yes?
- But half of 'em don't.

246
00:19:38,004 --> 00:19:40,005
- But half of 'em do.
- a man see.

247
00:19:40,006 --> 00:19:42,904
- Congratulations.
- I'm just sayin',

248
00:19:42,905 --> 00:19:43,905
I'm just sayin'.

249
00:19:44,873 --> 00:19:46,667
- Cheers.
- Yes, yes.

250
00:19:46,668 --> 00:19:47,496
Cheers.

251
00:19:50,879 --> 00:19:55,055
- Wedding dress shopping.
- Yeah!

252
00:20:44,519 --> 00:20:46,830
Hey, I thought you
were gonna wait for me.

253
00:20:46,831 --> 00:20:48,487
I didn't think you'd
be in any condition

254
00:20:48,488 --> 00:20:50,696
to run this mornin'.

255
00:20:50,697 --> 00:20:53,734
That sleep foam
mattress, I tell you.

256
00:20:53,735 --> 00:20:55,288
Yeah, I tell you.

257
00:20:56,151 --> 00:20:58,256
It's the best.

258
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:00,155
I need to get me one.

259
00:21:16,413 --> 00:21:18,897
So what do you think?

260
00:21:18,898 --> 00:21:20,899
I'm so proud of you.

261
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:22,970
It's not done yet but--

262
00:21:22,971 --> 00:21:26,042
It's time you got
back in the game.

263
00:21:26,043 --> 00:21:28,976
I have to admit,
sometimes I wonder.

264
00:21:28,977 --> 00:21:32,842
Who's gonna believe in you
if you don't believe in you?

265
