00:39:47,281 --> 00:39:48,109
No way.

530
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:56,703
These yams are really
good, Miss Ruthie.

531
00:39:56,704 --> 00:39:58,292
You did your thang.

532
00:39:59,397 --> 00:40:01,570
Look girl, you
ain't big as a minute.

533
00:40:01,571 --> 00:40:03,365
When you gonna have that baby?

534
00:40:03,366 --> 00:40:06,506
Not soon enough.

535
00:40:06,507 --> 00:40:11,373
Well at this rate I may
never have any grandchildren.

536
00:40:11,374 --> 00:40:12,374
You never know Miss Ruthie.

537
00:40:12,375 --> 00:40:13,583
You never know.

538
00:40:18,554 --> 00:40:20,347
I'm having a boy you know.

539
00:40:20,348 --> 00:40:22,109
Yeah, I can't wait.

540
00:40:22,972 --> 00:40:26,077
Want you to be the godfather.

541
00:40:26,078 --> 00:40:26,907
Hell yeah.

542
00:40:30,842 --> 00:40:31,670
Goddamn.

543
00:40:32,775 --> 00:40:34,293
Here come trouble.

544
00:41:07,050 --> 00:41:10,294
Man whatever you did, I
think she's done this time.

545
00:41:10,295 --> 00:41:12,297
It's what I didn't do.

546
00:41:20,961 --> 00:41:22,133
What could you
possibly tell me

547
00:41:22,134 --> 00:41:23,065
about Imani I
don't already know?

548
00:41:23,066 --> 00:41:25,482
Everybody has skeletons.

549
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:26,759
Everybody.

550
00:41:26,760 --> 00:41:28,036
So you better listen up.

551
00:41:28,037 --> 00:41:29,486
Okay but there's
nothing he can say

552
00:41:29,487 --> 00:41:31,142
that's gonna stop me from
wanting to marry her.

553
00:41:31,143 --> 00:41:31,972
Alright.

554
00:41:33,145 --> 00:41:34,630
What's the scheme?

555
00:41:36,079 --> 00:41:36,908
Imani?

556
00:41:39,048 --> 00:41:40,324
Imani is a good girl.

557
00:41:40,325 --> 00:41:42,464
Come on man, seriously?

558
00:41:43,673 --> 00:41:44,639
Her work shoes
stink but still,

559
00:41:44,640 --> 00:41:46,503
she's a good girl.

560
00:41:46,504 --> 00:41:47,918
So I'll buy some odor eaters.

561
00:41:50,438 --> 00:41:52,025
A little on the
chunky side too.

562
00:41:52,026 --> 00:41:53,855
I can live with that.

563
00:41:53,856 --> 00:41:55,097
Nobody's perfect.

564
00:41:55,098 --> 00:41:56,685
Not even my little Jasmyn.

565
00:41:56,686 --> 00:41:59,516
That's what I'm
talkin' about bro.

566
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:01,345
I'll kill you if
you ever mistreat her.

567
00:42:01,346 --> 00:42:02,484
Hmm?

568
00:42:02,485 --> 00:42:05,212
Ohh now that
sounds like a threat.

569
00:42:07,214 --> 00:42:09,491
Oh no, you can take
that to the bank.

570
00:42:09,492 --> 00:42:10,320
Cash it.

571
00:42:12,219 --> 00:42:14,634
Better watch it, dog.

572
00:42:14,635 --> 00:42:15,878
You be alright.

573
00:42:18,466 --> 00:42:22,609
we'll be back shortly.

574
00:42:25,197 --> 00:42:27,716
I can't believe I
let you talk me into this.

575
00:42:27,717 --> 00:42:29,546
I don't even like weddings.

576
00:42:29,547 --> 00:42:31,894
Just this one time for me.

577
00:42:33,516 --> 00:42:36,829
Alright, but you know
how i feel about it.

578
00:42:36,830 --> 00:42:39,866
It would mean the world to me.

579
00:42:39,867 --> 00:42:41,213
Your best man.

580
00:42:42,421 --> 00:42:44,250
Isn't that a little weird?

581
00:42:44,251 --> 00:42:45,665
No, this is my wedding.

582
00:42:45,666 --> 00:42:47,530
We're doing it my way.

583
00:42:48,773 --> 00:42:50,256
Alright.

584
00:42:50,257 --> 00:42:51,878
I'll be in your little wedding.

585
00:42:51,879 --> 00:42:53,778
Intimate, not little.

586
00:42:59,542 --> 00:43:01,854
Whoa yeah baby!

587
00:43:01,855 --> 00:43:03,925
Come on, seriously?

588
00:43:03,926 --> 00:43:06,099
That's what I'm talking about.

589
00:43:06,100 --> 00:43:07,273
You have to pay me.
- I ain't paying you.

590
00:43:07,274 --> 00:43:08,101
- You have to pay me.
- No.

591
00:43:18,009 --> 00:43:19,666
You must be Caleb.

592
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:22,254
Who wants to know?

593
00:43:26,051 --> 00:43:28,743
I'm here so apparently I do.

594
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:35,233
You should have expected me.

595
00:43:36,890 --> 00:43:40,065
Oh really?

596
00:43:42,585 --> 00:43:43,413
Really.

597
00:43:45,277 --> 00:43:47,382
Well you're here.

598
00:43:47,383 --> 00:43:50,765
So you already have your answer.

599
00:43:50,766 --> 00:43:52,043
So it's true.

600
00:43:54,839 --> 00:43:56,460
I'm asking.

601
00:44:02,709 --> 00:44:03,710
No wonder.

602
00:44:34,292 --> 00:44:36,638
What am I supposed to do?

603
00:44:36,639 --> 00:44:39,400
I can't leave him
here like this.

604
00:44:41,540 --> 00:44:44,302
I didn't say the
wedding was off.

605
00:44:47,581 --> 00:44:49,065
I don't know when.

606
00:44:57,591 --> 00:44:59,005
Remember what the Lord said

607
00:44:59,006 --> 00:45:00,558
to Moses about you and me

608
00:45:00,559 --> 00:45:02,560
when we had Kadesh Barnea.

609
00:45:02,561 --> 00:45:04,252
Caleb asked Joshua.

610
00:45:04,253 --> 00:45:05,460
And I brought him back a report

611
00:45:05,461 --> 00:45:07,773
according to my convictions.

612
00:45:07,774 --> 00:45:09,602
But my brothers,
who went up with me,

613
00:45:09,603 --> 00:45:12,225
made the hearts of the
people melt with fear.

614
00:45:12,226 --> 00:45:16,161
I have defiled the Lord,
my God wholeheartedly.

615
00:45:19,302 --> 00:45:22,926
You think I pulled
that name out of a hat?

616
00:45:22,927 --> 00:45:23,754
I would hope you
put more thought

617
00:45:23,755 --> 00:45:25,998
than that into it, dad.

618
00:45:25,999 --> 00:45:29,347
It takes courage
to follow your heart.

619
00:45:31,487 --> 00:45:34,041
Son, if you wanna paint, paint.

620
00:45:40,047 --> 00:45:44,637
Lucky for you it went in
through your shoulder.

621
00:45:44,638 --> 00:45:48,469
Lucky for me you're
not cashing in a policy.

622
00:45:51,783 --> 00:45:53,301
You need to eat something.

623
00:45:53,302 --> 00:45:55,027
It is not your job
to take care of me.

624
00:45:55,028 --> 00:45:56,546
I know it's not.

625
00:45:58,583 --> 00:46:01,931
You put your whole
life on hold for me.

626
00:46:04,244 --> 00:46:08,075
What's your fiance gonna
think about all that?

627
00:46:15,255 --> 00:46:19,258
I thought it'd be a good
idea to give Imani a break.

628
00:46:19,259 --> 00:46:22,780
You've been running
that poor girl ragged.

629
00:46:25,058 --> 00:46:28,751
Now don't you go feeling
sorry for yourself.

630
00:46:30,235 --> 00:46:34,238
I knew one day it
would come back on me.

631
00:46:34,239 --> 00:46:37,690
I just thought somehow it
would be tied to a fire.

632
00:46:37,691 --> 00:46:39,693
Mom, I feel like a fool.

633
00:46:41,591 --> 00:46:45,422
Baby, we've all been
there a time or two.

634
00:46:45,423 --> 00:46:46,803
The best part of
this whole thing

635
00:46:46,804 --> 00:46:48,944
is that you learn from it.

636
00:47:03,544 --> 00:47:05,201
Well I have to go.

637
00:47:07,169 --> 00:47:09,447
Don't look at me like that.

638
00:47:11,104 --> 00:47:14,865
Caleb, I have to
get back to my life.

639
00:47:14,866 --> 00:47:16,109
I understand.

640
00:47:23,254 --> 00:47:24,082
Go.

641
00:47:49,590 --> 00:47:52,040
Leave
a message at the tone.

642
00:47:52,041 --> 00:47:52,870
Hey.

643
00:47:54,423 --> 00:47:56,527
Thanks for the card.

644
00:47:56,528 --> 00:47:58,634
I wanted to say something

645
00:47:59,980 --> 00:48:02,395
that I didn't have
the heart to say

646
00:48:02,396 --> 00:48:03,742
a long time ago.

647
00:48:06,193 --> 00:48:09,093
I should have just
leveled with you

648
00:48:11,233 --> 00:48:12,820
I'm sorry, Breanna.

649
00:48:14,408 --> 00:48:16,583
I never meant to hurt you.

650
00:49:49,365 --> 00:49:52,437
There is no excuse
for what we did.

651
00:49:55,993 --> 00:49:58,616
If you blame anybody, blame me.

652
00:50:19,430 --> 00:50:21,638
Oh oh, the dead has arisen.

653
00:50:21,639 --> 00:50:23,191
- Ahhh.
- I'm sorry.

654
00:50:23,192 --> 00:50:24,468
Poor choice of words.

655
00:50:24,469 --> 00:50:26,229
Yeah, wrong shoulder too.

656
00:50:26,230 --> 00:50:27,437
My bad, my bad.

657
00:50:27,438 --> 00:50:29,059
What took you so long
to get over here?

658
00:50:29,060 --> 00:50:30,336
Everybody's been
asking about you.

659
00:50:30,337 --> 00:50:31,682
They wanna know when
you're coming back.

660
00:50:31,683 --> 00:50:34,685
I don't know if or
when I'm coming back.

661
00:50:34,686 --> 00:50:39,449
Thinking about taking on
this art thing full time.

662
00:50:39,450 --> 00:50:40,657
Well if you change your mind,

663
00:50:40,658 --> 00:50:43,177
we'll be happy to have you back.

664
00:50:43,178 --> 00:50:45,351
You know, I was thinking too.

665
00:50:45,352 --> 00:50:48,596
Not sure that I want my
boy to be a firefighter.

666
00:50:48,597 --> 00:50:49,873
I mean he'll be
fourth generation.

667
00:50:49,874 --> 00:50:53,118
I just want him to go
to school, you know.

668
00:50:53,119 --> 00:50:55,810
Come out an engineer,
a doctor or something.

669
00:50:55,811 --> 00:50:57,364
This is all I know.

670
00:50:59,884 --> 00:51:01,541
You gotta see Jasmyn.

671
00:51:02,404 --> 00:51:04,405
She's about ready to pop boy.

672
00:51:04,406 --> 00:51:06,579
- Yeah?
- Yeah man.

673
00:51:06,580 --> 00:51:09,306
Come on, let me get
you something to drink.

674
00:51:46,931 --> 00:51:47,759
Hello.

675
00:51:50,383 --> 00:51:51,487
Are you sure?

676
00:51:53,834 --> 00:51:54,835
First place?

677
00:51:56,906 --> 00:51:58,115
Yes, thank you!

678
00:52:21,172 --> 00:52:22,414
First place.
- Yeah.

679
00:52:22,415 --> 00:52:24,761
Hey don't forget about
us after you blow up.

680
00:52:24,762 --> 00:52:28,040
That'll be long
after he's dead.

681
00:52:28,041 --> 00:52:32,183
Guess that art degree is
worth somethin'.

682
00:52:33,460 --> 00:52:35,875
Or pursuin' your passion.

683
00:52:35,876 --> 00:52:38,430
- Cheers.
- Here, here.

684
00:52:55,586 --> 00:52:56,827
If you don't wanna do this,

685
00:52:56,828 --> 00:52:59,175
we can walk out
that door right now.

686
00:52:59,176 --> 00:53:04,007
I just realized that I'm
losing my best friend today.

687
00:53:04,008 --> 00:53:06,597
But you're gainin' a husband.

688
00:53:08,875 --> 00:53:11,360
Then why aren't you dressed?

689
00:53:17,746 --> 00:53:21,922
If you're not 100% sure
about a life-changing decision,

690
00:53:25,478 --> 00:53:27,825
you have time to reconsider.

691
00:53:38,974 --> 00:53:41,045
Havin' second thoughts?

692
00:53:42,702 --> 00:53:43,772
Relax, man.

693
00:53:45,532 --> 00:53:46,602
Relax, man.

694
00:53:50,157 --> 00:53:51,365
I just finished my residency.

695
00:53:51,366 --> 00:53:54,714
Ey, ey, at least you
got a great lawyer.

696
00:54:05,897 --> 00:54:07,451
What's the hold up?

697
00:54:32,407 --> 00:54:36,031
You know my timing
couldn't be any worse.

698
00:54:40,863 --> 00:54:42,037
Just say it.

699
00:54:44,591 --> 00:54:48,112
I was gonna leave
it alone, but I'm not.

700
00:54:52,185 --> 00:54:53,669
I love you, Imani.

701
00:55:22,698 --> 00:55:25,735
I can cut you a
deal on my retainer.

702
00:55:25,736 --> 00:55:27,012
Retainer, retainer?

703
00:55:27,013 --> 00:55:29,015
Man, what's the hold up?

704
00:55:30,327 --> 00:55:33,398
Ah ah, I would
advise you not to.

705
00:55:33,399 --> 00:55:36,746
Would you stop bein'
lawyer for one damn minute?

706
00:55:36,747 --> 00:55:38,265
What's goin' on?

707
00:55:40,440 --> 00:55:44,444
How much time we got?

708
00:55:45,687 --> 00:55:48,793
All is fair in
love and war, right?

709
00:55:50,036 --> 00:55:51,969
You crossed the line.

710
00:55:55,282 --> 00:55:57,284
This changes everything.

711
00:55:58,251 --> 00:55:59,665
I'm gonna find out for myself.

712
00:55:59,666 --> 00:56:00,942
No no no no no.

713
00:56:03,912 --> 00:56:08,088
C'mon, whoa whoa
whoa, ey.

714
00:56:10,470 --> 00:56:11,402
Okay, okay.

715
00:56:25,002 --> 00:56:27,003
Okay someone please
tell me what's goin' on.

716
00:56:27,004 --> 00:56:28,833
Yeah, tell us.

717
00:56:32,630 --> 00:56:35,702
♪ The thick and thin

718
00:56:36,565 --> 00:56:39,257
♪ When the fire

719
00:56:41,570 --> 00:56:44,021
♪ Freezes me

720
00:56:46,264 --> 00:56:48,542
♪ You'll be there

721
00:56:48,543 --> 00:56:51,924
I'm in love with
my best friend.

722
00:56:51,925 --> 00:56:54,030
♪ To Take my fear

723
00:56:54,031 --> 00:56:57,275
♪ And wash it all away

